  "body": "3.10.14 \"The unrestricted double type is a floating point numeric type that corresponds to the set of all possible double-precision 32 bit IEEE 754 floating point numbers, finite and non-finite. [IEEE-754]\"\n\nSurely this should read \"double-precision 64-bit floating point numbers\", matching the normal double definition, right?\n",
